//! n8n, Dify, agent package, Mermaid, and Web3 tools.

pub(in crate::operations::catalog) const N8N_INVENTORY: &str = "List n8n workflows, nodes, entry points, and analysis bounds from exported JSON already in the repository. path is an optional repository-relative file or path fragment; omit it to list every recognized export. A fragment can match tests/fixtures, and those files are real exports, not hidden. max_results is 1 to 500 and defaults to 200. bounds.found, bounds.shown, and bounds.truncated describe the page. An empty workflows array means nothing matched. Secrets stay off the graph. The tool does not call n8n and does not deploy a workflow.";

pub(in crate::operations::catalog) const N8N_TRACE: &str = "Upstream and downstream n8n port flow, output dependencies, and static subworkflow links for one node. label is required. A label that matches nothing returns state EMPTY, reason no matching node, and items []. An ambiguous label is an error that lists ids; pass one id. depth and max_nodes (1 to 500) bound the walk. cursor is the opaque page token from page.next_cursor, format v1:<offset>. Expression sites that are not proved stay explicit gaps. Secrets stay off the graph.";

pub(in crate::operations::catalog) const N8N_CONTEXT: &str = "Bounded n8n context for one node: proved dependencies, expression sites, and the unknowns that remain. label is required. A missing label returns state EMPTY. An ambiguous label is an error. task defaults to inspect and only keeps the bounded context on that question. max_related is 1 to 200 and defaults to 24. This is static export structure. It is not a workflow run.";

pub(in crate::operations::catalog) const DIFY_INVENTORY: &str = "List Dify apps, nodes, modes, and analysis bounds from exported YAML already in the repository. path is an optional repository-relative file or path fragment; omit it to list every recognized export. A fragment can match tests/fixtures. max_results is 1 to 500 and defaults to 200. An empty list means nothing matched. The tool does not call Dify and does not run an app.";

pub(in crate::operations::catalog) const DIFY_TRACE: &str = "Upstream and downstream Dify port flow, selectors, and typed data relations for one node. label is required. A label that matches nothing returns state EMPTY and items []. An ambiguous label is an error. Conversation variables are directed edges, and a string that merely contains the name is not a consumer. depth, max_nodes (1 to 500), and cursor (v1:<offset>) bound the walk.";

pub(in crate::operations::catalog) const DIFY_CONTEXT: &str = "Bounded Dify context for one node: proved consumers, selector sites, and explicit gaps. label is required. A missing label returns state EMPTY. An ambiguous label is an error. task defaults to inspect and only focuses the bound. max_related is 1 to 200 and defaults to 24. This reads the export. It does not execute the app.";

pub(in crate::operations::catalog) const AGENT_INVENTORY: &str = "List Agent Plugins, Skills, and MCP server bindings from local package files. Nothing is launched. path is an optional repository-relative plugin, skill, or MCP config fragment; omit it to list every recognized package file. A fragment can match tests/fixtures. max_results is 1 to 500 and defaults to 200. An empty list means no package file matched. Skill tool names are declared bindings, and they are not proved calls.";

pub(in crate::operations::catalog) const AGENT_TRACE: &str = "Declared origin, profile, transforms, and package bindings for one plugin, skill, or MCP server. label is required. A missing label returns state EMPTY. An ambiguous label is an error that lists ids. max_related caps the attached rows. Authorization that is not declared stays a gap. The tool does not start the server it describes.";

pub(in crate::operations::catalog) const AGENT_CONTEXT: &str = "Bounded agent-package context: declared bindings, source fragments, and explicit authorization gaps. label is required. A missing label returns state EMPTY. An ambiguous label is an error. task defaults to inspect and only focuses the bound. max_related is 1 to 200 and defaults to 24. allowed-tools hits are declarations. They are not proved calls into those tools.";

pub(in crate::operations::catalog) const AGENT_CHANGE_IMPACT: &str = "Compare two MCP catalog snapshots you supply and report contract changes, adapter compensation, and declared consumers. before and after are required repository-relative snapshot paths. A missing file matches no tools: the call still succeeds, changes is empty, and bounds.found is 0. That empty result is not a removal. A tool missing from a partial catalog is unconfirmed, and it is not removed. A schema change such as string to integer is incompatible. Duplicate tool labels are ambiguous-identity. max_results is 1 to 500 and defaults to 100. The tool does not launch either catalog.";

pub(in crate::operations::catalog) const DIAGRAM_INVENTORY: &str = "List Mermaid flowchart diagrams, native elements, and explicit sidecar bindings. path is an optional repository-relative Mermaid file, Markdown fence, or path fragment, and it can match tests/fixtures. max_results is 1 to 500 and defaults to 200. An empty list means no diagram matched. Arrows are not code calls.";

pub(in crate::operations::catalog) const DIAGRAM_TRACE: &str = "Walk declared_architecture arrows inside one Mermaid diagram. label is required. A missing label returns state EMPTY. An ambiguous label is an error. The hops are declared architecture, and they are never Calls. They do not clear dead code and they do not prove a production edge. depth, max_nodes (1 to 500), and cursor (v1:<offset>) bound the walk.";

pub(in crate::operations::catalog) const DIAGRAM_CONTEXT: &str = "Bounded Mermaid context: source fragments, explicit bindings, and gaps that remain unproved. label is required. A missing label returns state EMPTY. An ambiguous label is an error. task defaults to inspect. max_related is 1 to 200 and defaults to 24. An arrow without an explicit binding stays a gap.";

pub(in crate::operations::catalog) const WEB3_INVENTORY: &str = "List contract ABIs, compiler artifacts, and static viem or wagmi consumers that are already in the repository. No chain is contacted. path is an optional repository-relative ABI, artifact, or consumer fragment, and it can match tests/fixtures. max_results is 1 to 500 and defaults to 200. An empty list means nothing matched. Comment or string mentions are not consumers.";

pub(in crate::operations::catalog) const WEB3_TRACE: &str = "Walk proved ABI, artifact, and consumer bindings for one Web3 member or call site. label is required. A missing label returns state EMPTY. An ambiguous label is an error. depth, max_nodes (1 to 500), and cursor (v1:<offset>) bound the walk. A binding that is only a comment is not a consumer. Deployment is not queried.";

pub(in crate::operations::catalog) const WEB3_IMPACT: &str = "Compare two ABI revisions and report consumer-specific interface deltas, including silent event-misdecode risk. baseline and candidate are required repository-relative ABI or artifact paths. provider is an alias for candidate. A missing file still returns success: changes contains one row with kind missing_input, and that row is not MEMBER_REMOVED and not an empty ABI. When both files exist, each change names the member, whether the topic signature stayed the same, silent_misdecode, and the static consumers on those files. max_results is 1 to 500. task is stored and does not change the diff. bounds.deployment is not_provided. No chain is read.";

pub(in crate::operations::catalog) const WEB3_CONTEXT: &str = "Bounded Web3 context for one member: the ABI fragment, proved call or decoder sites, and explicit deployment gaps. label is required. A missing label returns state EMPTY. An ambiguous label is an error. task defaults to inspect. max_related is 1 to 200 and defaults to 24. Deployment and chain state are gaps unless the repository already contains that evidence. No RPC call is made.";
